figdown 0.1 bitfield
# `PRESENCE-CONDITION-EXPRESSION`: the positional PRESENCE FLAG is retired in both of its
# spellings. `optional` (…0.1, and again 0.1 after `PRESENCE-FLAG-SPELLING` reverted
# `PRESENCE-FLAG-SPELLING`) and `conditional` (0.1…0.1) are each a line error naming
# their migration; the live construct is the option key `present=`, whose
# VALUE is the presence condition. A bare flag could say only THAT a field
# was conditional — never why — so the condition had to live in note=, where
# neither the human nor the model could use it.
bitfield a "A" numbering=msb0 word=32
field "W" 16 present="C = 1"
field "X" 16 optional
field "Y" 16 conditional
field "Z" 16 present=""
